\> "Innovation thrives within the boundaries of mutual respect."

\>

\> This document outlines the legal architecture governing the use of SakiMCP. It reflects a synthesis of rigorous intellectual property standards and the agile spirit of modern software development.



\---



I. Preamble: The Bay Area-Bostonian Synthesis



Saki Studio, while headquartered in Taipei, operates under a global digital philosophy. We adopt a legal stance that merges Bostonian academic rigor with Bay Area innovation culture.



By accessing or installing SakiMCP, you acknowledge that you are entering into a binding agreement with Saki Studio, compliant with the Berne Convention and DMCA.



\---



II. Intellectual Property & Copyright



Proprietorship

The SakiLICENSE software suite, including its source code, compiled binaries, visual interface (UI/UX), and documentation, is the exclusive intellectual property of Saki Studio (Saki-tw).



Copyright © 2026 Saki Studio. All Rights Reserved.



Prohibitions

Without explicit written consent from Saki Studio:

1. Commercial Redistribution
2. Reverse Engineering
3. Attribution Removal



\---



III. End User License Agreement (EULA)



Saki Studio grants a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license for:



- Scope of Use：Personal, educational, or internal research.
- Fair Use & DMCA：Respect fair use; user is responsible for any infringement.



\---



IV. Disclaimer of Warranties ("AS-IS")



THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.



No liability for data loss, system instability, or business interruption.



\---



V. Open Source Compliance



SakiMCP incorporates open-source components under respective licenses (e.g., Apache 2.0, MIT).



\---



VI. Contact & Legal Notices



- Legal Dept: Saki@saki-studio.com.tw
- Web: https://saki-studio.com.tw



Saki Studio reserves the right to amend these terms.



